ember/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T17:58:19-07:00","id":188348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=188324#post188324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it'll be like Hunting Grounds: The rockies. But more stand aloneish, like Tribes or Signs.</div> </div> </div> </div> They'll be similar in concept to the locations in Blood and Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T17:59:34-07:00","id":188349,"title":"","content":"You'll find out more in two weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T18:02:53-07:00","id":188350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=188348#post188348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They'll be similar in concept to the locations in Blood and Smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Praise! That was my favorite chapter in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, and is actually my primary interest in the other Chronicle books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T18:05:21-07:00","id":188353,"title":"","content":"I like them.<br /> <br /> Resonance Shaper is going to get a lot of use in our game, I'm sure.<br /> But Sounds of the City, and Nowhere to run look great. Fading seems like it'd be fun as well, I could see it building up to the Surprise Attack as Rote Roll gift we saw in one of the previous blogs. The gift one.<br /> <br /> Imagining a section of merits like these the size of the one in Blood and Smoke puts a smile on my face.<br /> <br /> I'm glad Stew announced officially about the change in scheduling, and I can certainly appreciate not wanting to rehash the same old thing. But there's something to be said for the release of info. Hopefully we the fans will keep helping to get some word of mouth spread about the book. And it's always great to hear from the other developers, when they can talk. I'm sure everyone'd love to hear about the playtests, similar to Brookshaw's pre-Demon buildup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-04-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T19:55:45-07:00","id":188388,"title":"","content":"You know, it might be kind of cool if Forsaken Fridays and Supernal Saturdays were both every other week and alternated weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:09:47-07:00","id":188473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=188353#post188353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like them.<br /> <br /> Resonance Shaper is going to get a lot of use in our game, I'm sure.<br /> But Sounds of the City, and Nowhere to run look great. Fading seems like it'd be fun as well, I could see it building up to the Surprise Attack as Rote Roll gift we saw in one of the previous blogs. The gift one.<br /> <br /> Imagining a section of merits like these the size of the one in Blood and Smoke puts a smile on my face.<br /> <br /> I'm glad Stew announced officially about the change in scheduling, and I can certainly appreciate not wanting to rehash the same old thing. But there's something to be said for the release of info. Hopefully we the fans will keep helping to get some word of mouth spread about the book. And it's always great to hear from the other developers, when they can talk. I'm sure everyone'd love to hear about the playtests, similar to Brookshaw's pre-Demon buildup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once my playtest group gets back up and running again (due to the dreaded Real Life and various theatre obligations, we've been on a bit of hiatus), maybe I'll see if Stew is keen on me posting playtest reports in an Actual Play sort of style. Sort of like what I got to do for <b>Demon</b> for those who might remember my group's shenanigans running around Las Vegas. The <b>Werewolf</b> playtest game is set in the same continuity as the <b>Demon </b>game, and is in the city of Pittsburgh, PA. (For those familiar, the pack's territory is 'Sliberty - and yes, I said it that way on purpose.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:50:02-07:00","id":188504,"title":"","content":"I like Merits and all have been approved by Hamster. Well, Living Weapon is even made in to mu house rule, with all Uratha bites (beside Hishu) being Armor Piercing 1, just like announced Merit of higher of Wits and Dexterity in animal forms. And &quot;Shifting Fighting Style&quot; is real cool.<br /> <br /> But I have problem a bit with spoiler - almost all Auspices and Tribes got something cool for them to try in playtests. But not a single power both for Elodoth or Storm Lords. Our game Storm Lords Elodoth will be sad she can't try something cool for her character only. Also, this leads ther could be no &quot;social&quot; Werewolf's Merits - I get that this is game of savage fury, but one of 5 splats in it is more social one, and something social boosting would be fun for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T22:55:42-07:00","id":188524,"title":"","content":"The spoilers aren't meant to be playtest documents. There's no reason to assume that the Elodoth (who did get the Half Moon Gifts spoiled) and the Storm Lords are going to get shafted in the final book.<br /> <br /> As well, I don't think you can put a sole claim on any of them being &quot;more social.&quot; Sounds of the City is an Iron Master Merit... and it is most definitely social in function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T07:40:13-07:00","id":188689,"title":"","content":"There are social Merits - hell, the Iron Master previewed one basically is a social Merit - but obviously right now we're in redlines so I dunno what the final Merits list will include.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T17:51:44-07:00","id":189010,"title":"","content":"Damn these merits are awesome. Drafts or not I'm still going to use them in my game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:29:20-07:00","id":189026,"title":"","content":"The only criticism I really have is that the book is that the Iron Master and Hunter merits are too strong. At least they should be resisted in some way. Because as it is now, two werewolves look at you for a moment, and an hour later you've lost the job position you have worked 15 years for, and a monster knows where you and your family live. <br /> <br /> It is just too easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:43:44-07:00","id":189038,"title":"","content":"If you really want it to be harder, you could just have it contested or against their composure, if mortal, or supernatural power stat. Composure makes more sense, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-05-2014, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T20:15:18-07:00","id":189129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=189026#post189026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only criticism I really have is that the book is that the Iron Master and Hunter merits are too strong. At least they should be resisted in some way. Because as it is now, two werewolves look at you for a moment, and an hour later you've lost the job position you have worked 15 years for, and a monster knows where you and your family live.<br /> <br /> It is just too easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what temporary loss of Social Merits means and it's both silly and unhelpful to read them that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T20:34:02-07:00","id":189138,"title":"","content":"A temporary obstruction is not the same as complete loss. Basically you fluff it however you want, but all kinds of things can happen that makes it so your allies/contacts/retainers/whatever can't help you out for something, or the organization you're a part of is engaged in other matters and can't step in to assist you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T21:42:25-07:00","id":189168,"title":"","content":"I'm just curious how &quot;Sound of the City&quot; plays out in-setting. Do people have a magical (spirit-induced) compulsion to not return the target's calls, a malfunction at the bank causes his accounts to (temporarily) disappear, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T22:04:20-07:00","id":189195,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling Sound of the City is supposed to be flexible in how it looks in-character to allow different characters to display it differently. Maybe an Ithaeur causes spirit influenced loss of paper work, missed calls, and what not. While an Elodoth has offered people better offers or negotiated to get things tied up. Or a Rahu has intimidated people into not helping or actively obstruct the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T22:14:53-07:00","id":189202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=189195#post189195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling Sound of the City is supposed to be flexible in how it looks in-character to allow different characters to display it differently. Maybe an Ithaeur causes spirit influenced loss of paper work, missed calls, and what not. While an Elodoth has offered people better offers or negotiated to get things tied up. Or a Rahu has intimidated people into not helping or actively obstruct the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... but you don't need a merit to do those latter things. The merit presents it as something that happens automatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T22:30:51-07:00","id":189206,"title":"","content":"Shutting down the target's Merits takes a scene's worth of effort. It isn't an instant power where you snap your fingers and Resources doesn't work anymore.<br /> <br /> It does happen &quot;automatically&quot; in the sense of not needing to roll or using social Merits that can block other social Merits according to those systems. But it takes effort to make happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:20:51-07:00","id":189734,"title":"","content":"What Heavy Arms said. The drawback of losing access to your own social merits strongly suggests that that scene is spent wheeling and dealing, paying off people, having your own retainers tie up (not physically) the targets, etc. <br /> <br /> Same with the Hunter merit, reading it more carefully it doesn't tell the Hunter with a snap of a finger were their target is hiding, just a general idea of 'where' their hide-outs might be and some basic information about them. The roll is necessary to gain further information and who's to say whether you even uncover the correct safe house or bolt hole. Also there are further implications, what if the targets main safe house is in another packs territory and your Hunter just marked it?<br /> <br /> These merits are powerful there's no doubt, and there'll certainly be further revision. But they aren't without their limitations and a crafty GM could certainly play dirty with those drawbacks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T05:15:44-07:00","id":190155,"title":"","content":"These really are awesome merits, and I like how they essentially show how being an Uratha can vary from wolf to wolf. And the tribe merits, from the extremely fitting Iron Master stopgap to Hunters in the Darkness marking. Its a very cool feeling of the hunt, telling the prey they are marked.<br /> <br /> As for the Tactical Shifting merit? this has been needed for a while. One merit to focus all the tips and tricks of changing creatively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:19:40-07:00","id":190445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=189206#post189206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shutting down the target's Merits takes a scene's worth of effort. It isn't an instant power where you snap your fingers and Resources doesn't work anymore.<br /> <br /> It does happen &quot;automatically&quot; in the sense of not needing to roll or using social Merits that can block other social Merits according to those systems. But it takes effort to make happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you then say that these actions could be backtracked afterwards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:04:25-07:00","id":190489,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. The drawback doesn't do much if nobody can figure out that you're in a weaker spot while using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:26:51-07:00","id":190514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=190489#post190489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. The drawback doesn't do much if nobody can figure out that you're in a weaker spot while using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the only problem I have with the merit is the lack of real time constraint combined with zero ability to counter the merit. With minimal effort and no upkeep you can, for all intents and purposes, permanently take away merit dots. I don't really like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:40:21-07:00","id":190565,"title":"","content":"Or it could be limited to use ONLY during siskur-dah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T14:21:14-07:00","id":190726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=190514#post190514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the only problem I have with the merit is the lack of real time constraint combined with zero ability to counter the merit. With minimal effort and no upkeep you can, for all intents and purposes, permanently take away merit dots. I don't really like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That highly depends on how many Merit dots you have that the Drawback applies to I guess.<br /> <br /> I don't see all of your human sphere Merits being reduced by 1 for at long as you're upholding blocking someone's [Cunning] dots worth of Merits as being all that &quot;no upkeep&quot; for an Iron Master.<br /> <br /> You can only take away Merit dots as long as you're willing to lose Merit dots yourself. You can make sure you're losing less Dots than the other guy, but that means drastically limiting how many Merits you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T14:34:47-07:00","id":190755,"title":"","content":"I'm not too keen on the Hunter in Darkness or Iron Master merits either; partly because it's a power to take away people's options and it's rarely fun having your options taken away but mostly because they're powers that fit great for a &quot;tracker&quot; or a &quot;fixer&quot; charachter, that remove the need to actually track or fix things. Cutting someone off someone from their resources and allies is a complex bit of wheeling and dealing with a dramatic pay off. Why would you use a merit that automatically does that when you can role play it?<br /> <br /> Trying to find the spirit of Scrooge's bank account and threaten it, without the Spirit of MegaBank Plc noticing what you're doing to it's subjects is cool. Showing the bank manager just enough fang to get a 24 hour &quot;tempoary glitch in the system&quot; without going far enough to break the Oath of the Moon or attract hunters is cool. Compared to that, doing it automatically with a Merit just seems boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:01:37-07:00","id":190978,"title":"","content":"Nobody is gonna talk about how a gift given invisible character with Vanish in a room with 32 people will give -32 to be noticed after it wears off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:36:19-07:00","id":190997,"title":"","content":"Does Vanish still exist as a gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-07-2014, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T18:49:10-07:00","id":191002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=190755#post190755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you use a merit that automatically does that when you can role play it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because role-playing it every time probably isn't that interesting. And couldn't you say the same thing about most of the Merits this Merit acts on? Why buy Allies when you could just RP getting favors? Why buy Contacts when you could just RP talking to people?<br /> <br /> As well, the existence of the Merit doesn't preclude doing it the &quot;old fashioned&quot; way of RPing it. It's just another tool they can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T19:42:10-07:00","id":191031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=190726#post190726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That highly depends on how many Merit dots you have that the Drawback applies to I guess.<br /> <br /> I don't see all of your human sphere Merits being reduced by 1 for at long as you're upholding blocking someone's [Cunning] dots worth of Merits as being all that &quot;no upkeep&quot; for an Iron Master.<br /> <br /> You can only take away Merit dots as long as you're willing to lose Merit dots yourself. You can make sure you're losing less Dots than the other guy, but that means drastically limiting how many Merits you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you don't require Merit dots in human social spheres to take/use this merit. So you can quite easily make a character that can permanently take away merit dots for no const to themselves. Again, I don't like it. It for all intents and purposes reads, pay 2 merit dots to permanently remove 1-5 merit dots from your target. I feel like this sets a really bad precedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T22:02:47-07:00","id":191120,"title":"","content":"Not being able to take some of the most valuable/useful Merits in the game just to block of 1-5 dots of Merits against one target indefinitely is a pretty steep opportunity cost.<br /> <br /> I think you're really underestimating the drawback here. I think you're also fairly strongly overstating the impact of locking down someone's Merits. Most of those Merits can be blocked by Merit dot use away. You're treating the Renown factor here as effectively a non-issue even though Renown is more expensive than Merits are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T23:48:23-07:00","id":191152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=191120#post191120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being able to take some of the most valuable/useful Merits in the game just to block of 1-5 dots of Merits against one target indefinitely is a pretty steep opportunity cost.<br /> <br /> I think you're really underestimating the drawback here. I think you're also fairly strongly overstating the impact of locking down someone's Merits. Most of those Merits can be blocked by Merit dot use away. You're treating the Renown factor here as effectively a non-issue even though Renown is more expensive than Merits are.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only a steep cost only if you planned to take them before hand. If you didn't, you lose nothing, which is what I'm talking about. Not every character is going to have them, and I've seen and played a fair share that dont. This merit isn't as big a problem if you're playing a character who the drawback meaningfully affects, but as I've said, it isn't restricted to just them.<br /> <br /> And other merits don't suffer from the same problems this one does. They can be used in conjunction with actions taken in game to do these things but usually only if appropriate. And these things are also usually never automatic and steps can be taken to reclaim those dots, and if said dots can't be reclaimed, that's where the sanctity of merits comes in. That doesn't apply here. You can permanently lose merits without regaining those merits to use elsewhere. This breaks that sanctity for something that can effectively cost a character nothing outside of what they were already planning to get for other uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-08-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T01:54:14-07:00","id":191246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=191152#post191152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only a steep cost only if you planned to take them before hand. If you didn't, you lose nothing, which is what I'm talking about. Not every character is going to have them, and I've seen and played a fair share that dont. This merit isn't as big a problem if you're playing a character who the drawback meaningfully affects, but as I've said, it isn't restricted to just them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the nature of the Merit... I find it highly unlikely that a character that isn't interested in the affected Merits would also develop this Merit. Even if it doesn't have a mechanical prerequisite, the narrative one is obvious. How the hell does your character fit the fluff for this Merit without the other Merits in question?<br /> <br /> Pitch me the concept in which it is both appropriate that the character religiously avoids these Merits, and still has a reason to have learned Iron Master tricks for shutting down human assets. Because at the moment is sounds more like a player seeing the mechanics and wanting them, not something that makes any sense in character for the character to have learned how to do.<br /> <br /> Plenty of characters have no reason to invest in any those Merits... but they'd have the same reasons not to invest in this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can be used in conjunction with actions taken in game to do these things but usually only if appropriate. </div> </div> </div>Allies doesn't have a particularly strong restriction along these lines. If you want, you can use Allies 5 to shut down another character's Merit indefinitely as well as long as you don't ask any more of your Allies. There's no roll needed. And the target can't do anything to reclaim those dots besides get rid of you or block your Allies with something else.<br /> <br /> If someone is using Allies 5 to keep your Mentor in constant legal trouble, you don't get to use the Sanctity of Merits rules to trade your Mentor in for something else. You haven't lost your Mentor.<br /> <br /> Neither is actually permanent because both only last as long as the character with the Merit continues to use it to block. Stop that and the blocking stops and you get your Merit back in full force.<br /> <br /> As well, Allies isn't all or nothing. If you have Allies 5 and are blocking a 3 dot Merit, you still have 2 dots of favors to ask without getting into trouble. With the Iron Master Merit you can only block. If you can block more than the target has, the extra blocking power is wasted.<br /> <br /> Allies can also be bought multiple times, getting around any &quot;this group couldn't do that&quot; issues, and giving you the ability to block even more dots, against even more characters. The Iron Master Merit can't. It'll only ever block one target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T04:18:05-07:00","id":191293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=190514#post190514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the only problem I have with the merit is the lack of real time constraint combined with zero ability to counter the merit. With minimal effort and no upkeep you can, for all intents and purposes, permanently take away merit dots. I don't really like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Maybe cost it with Willpower points. With GMC combat makes you almost every turn to spend Willpower, it;s a <b>huge</b> cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T07:27:55-07:00","id":191366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/188301-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-merits?p=191293#post191293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Maybe cost it with Willpower points. With GMC combat makes you almost every turn to spend Willpower, it;s a <b>huge</b> cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I concede the point. I forget how overly strong some GMC merits are, but if these are the new standards these are the new standards. That said, the ease in which you can have these merits robbed from you nowadays makes me really hesitant to take them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T08:25:34-07:00","id":191412,"title":"","content":"To be fair, you can only block up to five dots of Merits at a time with Pulse of the City, and while you're doing so, all of your own social Merits are considered one dot lower. Even if you build a character with no social merits, you're still trading two of your own Merit dots to block five dots total of other people's Merits, assuming you have Cunning 5. That's only a net 3xp advantage, and only if your character is built to use this specific Merit to maximum effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}